## Context

`tests/test_validate.sh` lines 600-619 had a double-run anti-pattern: the
WARNING tests ran `erg validate` twice — once with `|| true` to capture output,
then again to check exit code. This is redundant and wasteful. The non-.erg
variant also had inverted nesting (exit-code check wrapping the grep instead of
the other way round).

## Actions

Replace with single-run pattern: `out=$(...) && rc=0 || rc=$?` which captures
output AND preserves the real exit code under `set -e`.

## Exit criteria

- Each WARNING test invokes `erg validate` exactly once
- `make test-validate` passes (36/36)
